# verify-emit-allow.diffpatterns — intentional emit-vs-live deltas, each justified.
#
# Consumed by scripts/dev/verify-emit.sh. Line format:
#     <tile>|<file>|<extended-regex>
# tile = tile-dir name or *;  file = tile.env | qemu-streamhost.sh | x11-runtime.sh | *.
# The regex matches a whole diff CONTENT line INCLUDING its prefix:
#     "< " = the line exists only in the LIVE file (superseded by the repo)
#     "> " = the line exists only in the EMITTED/repo file (repo is ahead)
# Every entry must carry a one-line justification comment directly above it.
# An unexplained diff line fails the gate — do NOT add entries without a reason.
#
# EMPTY since 2026-08-11: the full-fleet re-emit that followed the drift sweep
# (registry learned SH_BUFSIZE_RATIO / SH_ABS_PACE_MS / SH_WARPD_PACE_MS /
# SH_ENCODER_PRESET; win2000 + redstar2 fixtures harvested) cleared every
# whitelisted delta — the gate now expects byte parity fleet-wide. Add rows
# only for NEW deliberate divergence, never to silence drift.
